  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_019, acc=0.639) uses pca_n2000 as the RNA encoder, and all six completed experiments share this encoder. The key unexplored dimension is whether a learned RNA representation (scvi_n200) can improve upon PCA in the multimodal setting. Config_031 tests scvi_n200 while holding all other settings at their empirically best values (multiprofile, resnet50, avgpool aggregation, weighted fusion). This is the highest-information experiment because: (1) it directly addresses the largest remaining uncertainty—whether the RNA bottleneck is the encoder or something else; (2) if scvi_n200 improves, it opens a strong exploitation path; if it does not, we can rule out learned RNA encoders as a lever and focus remaining budget on other axes; (3) compared to testing transformer+weighted (config_021), which is unlikely to beat avgpool+weighted given the 4-point gap already observed with concat, the RNA encoder question has far greater potential to shift the performance landscape."
}

